## X1. What an Antigravity session is told about listening
$ (A) handoff role reviewer   (the Listening line)
Listening: Run `handoff wait --for reviewer --timeout 60m` in the background. Exit 3: run it again. Exit 4: something else already listens for reviewer, perhaps your own earlier wait. After you handle what it delivers, wait again. In Antigravity, that is `run_command` with a short `WaitMsBeforeAsync`, so the command goes to the background and its exit wakes you with what it printed. If none runs when your turn ends and your session has handoff's hooks, a hook listens for reviewer, but it can wake you only 10 times before the operator types in this session.
$ (A, SessionStart hook) handoff hook brief   (the Listening line)
Listening: Run `handoff wait --for reviewer --timeout 60m` in the background. Exit 3: run it again. Exit 4: something else already listens for reviewer, perhaps your own earlier wait. After you handle what it delivers, wait again. In Antigravity, that is `run_command` with a short `WaitMsBeforeAsync`, so the command goes to the background and its exit wakes you with what it printed. If none runs when your turn ends, a hook listens for reviewer, but it can wake you only 10 times before the operator types in this session.
$ handoff brief --for reviewer   (by hand, no session: the Listening line)
Listening: In Claude Code, run `handoff wait --for reviewer --timeout 25m` in the background. Exit 3: run it again. Exit 4: something else already listens for reviewer, perhaps your own earlier wait. After you handle what it delivers, wait again. In Codex, don't run wait, since each minute of it costs a whole model call: end your turn. If work waits for you, the operator hears of it and tells you.
-- a Claude Code session with hooks, for comparison:
Listening: you don't run `handoff wait`. When your turn ends, a hook listens for implementer and brings you what arrives.

## X2. The background wait: its exits, and the Stop hook beside it
$ (A) handoff wait --for reviewer --timeout 2s   (nothing new)
  [exit 3]
  binding A: block: none | listened: yes
posted #1 note P1 implementer → reviewer: one
$ (A) handoff wait --for reviewer --timeout 5s   (a note waits)
#1 note P1 implementer → reviewer: one
  [exit 0]
-- a wait runs in the background; the turn ends, and the Stop hook runs with fullyIdle false, then (were it true) beside the wait's lock:
$ (Antigravity A, Stop hook, executionNum 0, fullyIdle false) handoff hook listen --timeout 2s
    (no wake) | 
$ (Antigravity A, Stop hook, executionNum 0, fullyIdle true) handoff hook listen --timeout 2s
    (no wake) | 
$ (Antigravity A, Stop hook, executionNum 10, fullyIdle true) handoff hook listen --timeout 2s
    (no wake) | 
  binding A: block: none | listened: yes
